*******Then manually add*******:
JJWT dependencies
***************************************************
(JJWT is a third-party library and not a Spring Boot starter,
    so it does NOT appear in Initializr.)
***************************************************
JJWT (Java JWT library) is:
A pure Java library
Used to create and validate JWT tokens
Not officially maintained by Spring
That’s why you must add it manually in pom.xml.

*****Why did you add 3 dependencies for JWT?****
You should say:
jjwt-api → JWT core API
jjwt-impl → Implementation (runtime only)
jjwt-jackson → JSON serializer/deserializer

***************************************************
Spring Security itself does NOT generate JWT.
It only provides security framework.
JWT generation must be done using:
JJWT
or Nimbus JOSE
or Auth0 Java JWT


